"dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-cap30-b2/cap30-44/omp-44/cells/without/trig-omp-multistep/28/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.3.0 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/7dd20b952257a3355c728716113cff772f7c5185/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Root cause: `to_cents` truncates float error (`int(19.99 * 100)` \u2192 `1998`). Rounding to the nearest cent fixes it.\nFixed. The bug was in `ledger/currency.py`, in `to_cents`. It used `int(amount * 100)`, which drops the fractional part instead of rounding, so tiny float errors lost a cent: `19.99 * 100` is `1998.999\u2026`, which came out as `1998`. The same thing happened with `0.29` and `4.35`.\n\nThe fix changes that line to `return round(amount * 100)`, which rounds to the nearest cent.\n\npytest isn't installed here, so I ran each test function directly with `python3`. All 4 tests in `tests/test_totals.py` and the one in `tests/test_report.py` pass.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": 6, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 64131, "requests_cache_write": 11519, "requests_cost_usd": 0.0898172, "requests_count": 6, "requests_input_uncached": 14, "requests_output": 967, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial28", "run_seed": 20261014, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 54, "score": 1.0, "started